The fresh false-result mutation built successfully and failed for the expected semantic reason: on the satisfying empty input, execution produced an empty heap list while the mutated target demanded an appended zero; `kprove` exited 1 with `WarnStuckClaimState`. A separate `> 0`→`> 1` body mutation also built and failed at the mismatched loop obligation, confirming that the proof is sensitive to the submitted body. I’ve found no false proof-local rule; the remaining issues are scope/bridge limitations, so I’m preparing a `CONCERNS / LEGIT` report rather than treating them as unsoundness.
